; --- The two fences ---------------------------------------------------------------
; ⚠️ ONE INTERACTABLE EACH (a DialogueComponent), trade behind DialogueEffect.OpenShop — 38E's rule,
; and it applies here for 38E's reason: GetComponent<T> returns the first child match, so a
; VendorComponent stacked on a talking merchant is a component that never fires. Both of these have
; conversations worth protecting, so both take the dialogue route.
;
; ⚠️ NO NEW BODIES. Sedge wears npc_hooded — the same hood the gate-hand wears at the Crossway, and
; that echo is deliberate: they are the same trade on opposite sides of the same road. Coyle wears
; npc_merchant_m. Neither wears npc_townsman (a hi-vis vest and a hard hat) or npc_merchant_f (a
; t-shirt and trainers); both are retired, and the second one took three sub-phases to catch.
; ⚠️ SHE STOOD IN THE LAKE FROM THE 2026-08-29 OVERHAUL TO 2026-08-31. Her berth was local
; (-17, 3) — authored when this district was a flat floor with translucent boxes on it for water.
; The overhaul carved the open water into a real 4.5 m basin and conformed every node onto the
; terrain under it, so she went down with the ground: 2.83 m under a declared surface, in a game
; with no swimming, with her map pin under it too. She now stands at the spine's west end, the
; last dry ground before her berth, north of the road and opposite Coyle exactly as the note
; above says. Ground here is +0.30 against a 0.05 waterline, and the whole district is that flat:
; ⚠️ A NODE MOVED MORE THAN A METRE WEST OF x = -13 IS IN THE WATER AGAIN.
[node name="Sedge" type="Node3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, -1, 0, 0, -12, 0, -0.5)
script = ExtResource("2_entity")
DisplayName = "Sedge Marrow"
TemplateId = "npc.sedge"

